event: text.replace
data: {"Type":"text.replace","MessageId":"rpl_1bx_20261013_235217_400_CroBQXwS","ContentIndex":0,"Text":"After a chilled water leak, the Licensed Electrical Worker (LEW) must approve re-energising the affected electrical equipment . The evidence required before that approval is: LEW sign-off, insulation resistance test passed, and the area confirmed dry . All three must be confirmed; re-energisation is blocked if any required evidence is missing .\n\nRule TS-07, pill version 1.2.0 .","Timestamp":"1791906741062","RecordId":""}

event: message.done
data: {"Type":"message.done","MessageId":"rpl_1bx_20261013_235217_400_CroBQXwS","Message":{"Type":"reply","MessageId":"rpl_1bx_20261013_235217_400_CroBQXwS","Name":"reply","Title":"","Icon":"","Status":"success","StatusDesc":"Reply Completed","Contents":[{"Type":"text","Text":"After a chilled water leak, the Licensed Electrical Worker (LEW) must approve re-energising the affected electrical equipment . The evidence required before that approval is: LEW sign-off, insulation resistance test passed, and the area confirmed dry . All three must be confirmed; re-energisation is blocked if any required evidence is missing .\n\nRule TS-07, pill version 1.2.0 ."}],"ExtraInfo":{"Elapsed":"8","StartTime":"1791906741059","EndTime":"1791906741067"},"RecordId":""},"Timestamp":"1791906741067","RecordId":""}

event: response.completed
data: {"Type":"response.completed","Response":{"Role":"assistant","RecordId":"1bx_20261013_235217_400_CroBQXwS","RelatedRecordId":"0b5_20261013_235217_338_aA27Eee4","ConversationId":"d4a0637f88614a94a962b98325fd5ced","Status":"success","StatusDesc":"Calling the knowledge base","Messages":[{"Type":"reply","MessageId":"rpl_1bx_20261013_235217_400_CroBQXwS","Name":"reply","Title":"","Icon":"","Status":"success","StatusDesc":"Reply Completed","Contents":[{"Type":"text","Text":"After a chilled water leak, the Licensed Electrical Worker (LEW) must approve re-energising the affected electrical equipment . The evidence required before that approval is: LEW sign-off, insulation resistance test passed, and the area confirmed dry . All three must be confirmed; re-energisation is blocked if any required evidence is missing .\n\nRule TS-07, pill version 1.2.0 ."}],"ExtraInfo":{"Elapsed":"8","StartTime":"1791906741059","EndTime":"1791906741067"},"RecordId":""}],"Procedures":[{"Name":"knowledge","Title":"Calling the knowledge base","Status":"success","IntentCate":"Documentation Q\u0026A","ResourceStatus":0,"Type":"knowledge","Knowledge":{"Content":"After a chilled water leak, who must approve re-energising the affected electrical equipment, and what evidence is required before that approval? Cite the rule id and pill version.","RewriteQuery":"","Outputs":[{"Type":2,"Content":"File name: keystone-chilled-water-leak-knowledge\nPassage: \n### TS-07 — No re-energisation without LEW sign-off\n\n- **Pill version:** 1.2.0\n- **Action class:** Must Escalate\n- **Owner:** Chief Engineer\n- **Escalate to:** Duty LEW, falling back to Head Technical Services\n- **Required evidence (ALL must be confirmed):** lew_signoff, insulation_resistance_ok, area_dry\n- **BLOCKED if any required evidence is missing.**\n\n\nDecision: Re-energise affected AHU, DB, or circuit only after LEW inspection and certification. LEW inspects, tests insulation resistance, documents fitness. Technical Services restores in sequence. FCC confirms alarms normal. No re-energisation on visual inspection alone.\n\nAllowed:\n\n- Keep circuit isolated\n- Request LEW inspection\n- Staged re-energisation on LEW certification\n- Alarm verification via FCC\n\n\nForbidden:\n\n- Re-energise before LEW sign-off\n- Re-energise on visual inspection alone\n- Re-energise before the room is dry\n- Reset a tripped breaker before LEW tests insulation resistance\n\n\nExceptions:\n\n- Critical facilities manager co-signs the LEW sign-off before return to service; the client SLA notice goes via the CFM (TS-10, TE-06)\n"},{"Type":2,"Content":"File name: keystone-chilled-water-leak-knowledge\nPassage: \n### Electrical safety\n\n- If water is \n- in, above, or flowing toward\n-  an electrical\n-  room,\n- switchroom, riser cupboard, or lift motor room — \n- nobody enters\n- .\n-  The\n- Licensed Electrical Worker (LEW) tests and signs off the\n-  affected\n- electrical installation before re-energisation (EMA LEW\n-  regime).\n- Do \n- not\n-  shut down a whole floor's power unless the electrical risk\n-  is\n- confirmed by the LEW or by clear evidence (water on switchgear,\n-  breaker\n- tripped, insulation resistance below threshold). A false power-down on\n-  a\n- bank anchor tenant's trading floor is a seven-figure incident in its\n-  own\n- right.\n- A tripped breaker is evidence of risk, but nobody resets it — and\n-  nobody\n- widens the power-down on the strength of it — until the LEW has\n-  inspected\n- the tripped circuit (TS-03 adds \n- `lew_inspected_tripped_breaker`\n-  as\n- required evidence). The reset itself is a re-energisation \n- (TS-07).\n- Re-energisation after any wetting event requires: LEW\n-  sign-off,\n- insulation resistance test passed, and the area confirmed dry.\n-  No\n- exceptions. The gate in TS-07 blocks this\n-  unconditionally.\n"},{"Type":2,"Content":"File name: keystone-chilled-water-leak-knowledge\nPassage: \n## How to use this pill\n\n- Incident mode\n-  — When an incident is declared (iBMS leak alarm,\n-  tenant\n- call, security patrol report), feed the evidence map to \n- `rules.yaml`\n- .\n- Evidence keys are the vocabulary declared in \n- `evidence.yaml`\n-  (label,\n-  type,\n- who may confirm each item). A required item counts only when it\n-  is\n- confirmed and true; an unknown fact is simply\n-  absent.\n- The deterministic engine evaluates each rule's \n- `trigger`\n-  conditions\n-  against\n- the evidence and produces action chips: \n- Recommend\n- , \n- Requires approval\n- ,\n- or \n- Must escalate\n- .\n- Why drawer\n-  — For every action, the host can surface: the rule ID,\n-  the\n- pill version, the evidence items used, the missing evidence, the\n-  owner,\n- the escalation target, and the provenance (transcript quote +\n-  timestamp).\n- Counterfactual\n-  — \"What would change this decision?\" is answered\n-  by\n- listing the unmet evidence items and exception conditions in each\n-  rule.\n"},{"Type":2,"Content":"File name: keystone-chilled-water-leak-knowledge\nPassage: \n### TS-03 — Do not shut down whole floor power unless electrical risk confirmed\n\n- **Pill version:** 1.2.0\n- **Action class:** Requires Approval\n- **Owner:** Technical Services Lead\n- **Escalate to:** Duty LEW, falling back to Head Technical Services\n- **Required evidence (ALL must be confirmed):** lew_or_evidence_confirms_risk\n- **BLOCKED if any required evidence is missing.**\n\n\nDecision: Do not shut down a whole floor's power based on a tenant request or a precautionary instinct. Power-down only when electrical risk is confirmed by the LEW or by clear evidence: water on switchgear, breaker already tripped, or insulation resistance below threshold. A false power-down on a bank anchor tenant's trading floor is a seven-figure incident.\n\nAllowed:\n\n- Send technician to assess with moisture meter\n- Request LEW inspection if risk uncertain\n- Isolate individual affected circuit on LEW advice\n\n\nForbidden:\n\n- Shutting down a whole floor on tenant request alone\n- Shutting down a whole floor without LEW or confirmed evidence\n- De-energising circuits not in the water path\n\n\nExceptions:\n\n- Breaker already tripped — the LEW inspects the tripped circuit before any reset or wider power-down (a reset is a re-energisation, TS-07)\n"},{"Type":2,"Content":"File name: keystone-chilled-water-leak-knowledge\nPassage: # Keystone Intelligence Pill — chilled-water-leak v1.2.0\n\nApproved pill exported from Keystone on 2026-10-13. This is the authoritative sourcefor chilled-water leak response. Cite the rule ID and the version 1.2.0 exactly aswritten below. Do not paraphrase a rule ID and never invent a version number.\n\n---"}]}}],"StatInfo":{"InputTokens":0,"OutputTokens":0,"TotalTokens":2132,"TotalCost":"3731"},"ExtraInfo":{"RequestId":"bf6c9908bc124be6ae9567ed73cff8f3","TraceId":"2df67862f9ae75969214aef45bbb6601 / 1bx_20261013_235217_400_CroBQXwS","Elapsed":"3645","StartTime":"1791906737336","IsFromSelf":false,"IsLlmGenerated":true,"CanRating":true,"CanFeedback":false,"ReplyMethod":12,"FromName":"Keystone Pill Agent","FromAvatar":"https://lke-intl-1251316161.cos.ap-jakarta.myqcloud.com/%2Fpublic/2109948037519756224/2109949475796942208/image/KDokpwaApGYmpBPMDHt-2109949477629853056.png","HasRead":false,"EndTime":"1791906741067"}},"Timestamp":"1791906741068","RecordId":""}

